 Options:
 
-- `limit` (positive integer, required) — requests allowed per key per window.
-- `windowMs` (positive integer, required) — window length.
-- `now` (function, optional) — clock, defaults to `Date.now`. Windows start at multiples of `windowMs`.
+- `limit` (positive integer, required): default requests allowed per key per window.
+- `windowMs` (positive integer, required): window length in milliseconds.
+- `now` (function, optional): clock, defaults to `Date.now`. Windows start at multiples of `windowMs`.
+- `overrides` (object or `Map`, optional): key-to-limit mapping that replaces `limit` for those keys. Each value must be a positive integer. Only own enumerable string properties of an object are used; a `Map` supports arbitrary keys. The mapping is copied when the limiter is created.
+
+Methods:
+
+- `tryAcquire(key)`: consumes one request and returns `true` if the key has budget; otherwise returns `false` without consuming budget.
+- `remaining(key)`: returns the key's unused requests in the current window without consuming budget. Returns zero when exhausted and the full applicable limit for an unused key or at the start of a new window. Each key has an independent budget.
